# =============================================================================
# Bibliometric Analysis
# 
# 
# What this script does
#   • Queries PubMed for yearly publication counts from 1990–2025
#   • Generates trend plots for depression, antidepressants, immune response,
#     neuroimmune terms, cytokines and immune-cell markers
#   • Builds heatmaps summarizing publication frequency across selected topics
#   • Extracts author-affiliation countries from PubMed records and creates a
#     world map of publication distribution
#   • Generates a keyword word cloud based on PubMed term frequencies
#   • Saves all figures as high-resolution TIFF files for manuscript use
#
# How to use
#   1) Install the required R packages listed in the setup section.
#   2) Set your project/output directory and, if needed, adjust the PubMed queries.
#   3) Run the script in R or RStudio.
#   4) For the world map step, review and correct the exported country table
#      before generating the final map.
#
# Notes: PubMed counts may change over time, 2025 may be incomplete, and country
# assignments from affiliations should be manually checked before interpretation.
#
# =============================================================================

